name: Alert
canonical_in_docs: true
canonical_candidate: false
description: 'Platform-detected and externally-injected issues against catalog entities,
  including failed jobs, data-quality test failures, schema incompatibilities, and
  distribution anomalies. Three visibility scopes: All / My Objects (owner-linked)
  / Dependents (downstream-by-lineage). Alert lifecycle: OPEN (Platform creates) →
  RESOLVED (Operator) / RESOLVED_AUTOMATICALLY (Platform when condition clears). **Batch
  H** adds the PRIMARY-SOURCE persistence layer via ReactiveAlertRepositoryImpl —
  19-method repository owning every ALERT and ALERT_CHUNK SQL operation. SQL-level
  confirmation of REFACTOR-024: `listAllWithStatusOpen` at line 143-145 is `selectFrom(ALERT).where(ALERT.STATUS.eq(OPEN))`
  with NO owner predicate, NO permission filter, NO role check. Repository carries
  no @ReactiveTransactional; transactions live at AlertServiceImpl. `getOpenAlertsForEntities`
  is the ONLY method using FOR UPDATE (line 133 — explicit comment frames the FDQT
  ingestion-race intent); the mutation path (`updateAlertStatus`, `resolveAutomatically`)
  has NO FOR UPDATE — deliberate asymmetry. `createAlerts` issues `INSERT ... RETURNING`
  with NO ON CONFLICT — AlertManager webhook retries can produce duplicate alerts.
  NEW batch-H bug: `listByOwner` at line 177 uses platform-wide `countAlertsWithStatusOpen()`
  as empty-result counter, not owner-scoped variant — UI badge misreports total when
  owner has zero alerts. (AlertController + alert openapi-tag + alerts route + ReactiveAlertRepositoryImpl
  sidecars.)'
